<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong, Wako set $50mln fund.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong, Wako set $50mln fund.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Ssangyong Investment and Securities Co Ltd and Japan's Wako Securities Co Ltd launched a $50 million fund on Friday for investment on the Seoul stock exchange, a Ssangyong Securities statement said.</p>
<p>The Korea Active Fund will begin trading from October 25 and will focus on shares with no over-the-counter premium. The fund will be managed by Ssangyong Investment Management Co Ltd.</p>
<p>The statement said most of the fund will be mobilised by Japanese investors.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
